24. DISPUTE RESOLUTION; MANDATORY ARBITRATION; CLASS ACTION WAIVER

PLEASE READ THIS SECTION CAREFULLY. IT AFFECTS YOUR LEGAL RIGHTS, INCLUDING YOUR RIGHT
TO FILE A LAWSUIT IN COURT AND TO HAVE A JURY TRIAL.

To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, any dispute, claim, or controversy
arising out of or relating to this Agreement, the Software, or the Service shall be
resolved by final and binding individual arbitration administered under the rules of a
recognized arbitration provider, before a single arbitrator, seated in Wyoming, and
governed by the Federal Arbitration Act.

TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, EACH PARTY WAIVES ANY RIGHT TO BRING OR
PARTICIPATE IN A CLASS, COLLECTIVE, CONSOLIDATED, OR REPRESENTATIVE ACTION. The
arbitrator may not consolidate claims or preside over any form of representative
proceeding.

Notwithstanding the foregoing, either party may (a) bring an individual claim in small
claims court, and (b) seek temporary or permanent injunctive or other equitable relief
in a court of competent jurisdiction to protect intellectual property, confidential
information, or trade secrets, without first submitting to arbitration.

This section does not apply to the extent applicable law prohibits its enforcement,
and shall not apply to any User to whom mandatory arbitration or class-action waiver
is unenforceable under mandatory consumer-protection law in that User's jurisdiction.
If this section is held unenforceable in whole or in part, the remainder of this
Agreement remains in effect and disputes shall proceed under section 23.

